ulator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and November to December came in under 90% of normal in 40 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025, the middle of the grids got 171% of normal in April to May and 34% in November to December. The preliminary estimate for grid 18740 in August to September 2026 is 30.0, a figure from NOAA rain that RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ from. Every grid had its driest year in 1963, with grid 18440 at 45%.</p>"}
